# SensorReadingReport: generated by tools/generate_interfaces.py from more_generic_models 0.1.0. Do not edit.
# One reading of one of the vehicle's own sensors (never the truth), as the vehicle's navigation sees it, one record for every
# sensor. ``sensor`` the reading's ``Measurement.sensor`` kind, ``kind`` what it is (``attitude``, ``angular_rate``,
# ``acceleration``, ``heading``, ``magnetic_field``, ``satellite_position``, ``depth``, ``ground_velocity``, ``water_velocity``,
# ``range``, ``speed``) and ``values`` its named numbers (units and keys per kind: ``vehicle_api/sensor_readings.py`` and the
# README). ``covariance`` the reading's covariance (None: none), ``frame`` its frame as the sensor states it, ``measured_at`` the
# instant the reading is valid for (s on the scenario clock) and ``t`` the sample that issued the report. ``valid`` is False for a
# reading the sensor marks invalid and for one older than the API's ``max_age`` for that sensor; every value is then NaN and
# ``measured_at`` still says how old it was: a stale reading is never held as a current one.
#
# Frames (owner decision): positions NED about the scenario origin (x north, y east), body quantities FRD, angles in rad from
# north clockwise, time in s on the scenario clock.
std_msgs/Header header  # stamp = t rounded to ns; frame_id map_ned for positions
uint64 stream_seq  # publication counter per vehicle across all report types (restores the drain order)
float64 t  # unit: s; the sample instant on the scenario clock, exactly
string sensor  # unit: enum
string kind  # unit: enum
StrFloat[] values  # unit: mixed; frame: reading; named numbers, unit per key and kind: ``sensor_readings.py``
float64[<=9] covariance  # square matrix, row-major, size 1 or 2 or 3; unit: mixed; frame: reading; numpy array of shape (n, n), the reading's R for its n rows, in the squared units of the rows (shapes per kind: sensor_readings.py); None: none
string frame  # unit: text; the reading's own frame word
bool valid  # unit: flag
float64 measured_at  # unit: s
